INPUT FOR MONTE CARLO RADIATIVE TRANSFER PROGRAM 
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
GRID PARAMETERS
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
30                      :number of columns in horizontal x direction   
20                      :number of columns in horizontal y direction   
33                      :number of layers in vertical z direction      
120.0                   :dimension of domain in horizontal x direction 
80.0                    :dimension of domain in horizontal y direction 
1                       :location of the light source, TOA (1) or surface (0) 
1                       :location of the detector, TOA (1) or surface (0) 
1                       :definition of output nx*ny grid, surface (0) or TOA (1), only matters for 3D case and VZA>0 deg 
 
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
MONTE CARLO PARAMETERS
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
5000                    :number of photons per column per round        
100                     :maximum number of rounds                      
.false.                 :stop simulation when result has converged     
0.001                   :if .true., maximum allowed reflectance standard deviation 
 
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
GENERAL PARAMETERS
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
3                       :size of Stokes vector (1, 3, or 4)            
wl                      :use wavelength (wl) in nm or wavenumber (wn) in cm-1 
340.000                 :min wav of the light (nm or cm-1)             
340.000                 :max wav of the light (nm or cm-1)             
1.000                   :wav step size (nm or cm-1)                    
.false.                 :read gas scat. optical thickness bmsca from file? 
bmsca.dat               :if .true., what is the bmsca filename?        
0                       :if .false., inside layer assume hydrostat. equil. (1) or exp. density decay (0)  
Earth                   :if .false., which planet (for depol. factor and refr. index), Earth or Venus? 
.false.                 :use fixed depolarization factor? If .false. it is computed from wavelength 
0.03                    :if .true., what is the fixed depolarization factor? 
.false.                 :read gas abs. optical thickness bmabs from file? 
bmabs.dat               :if .true., what is the bmabs filename?        
baer                    :type of cloud input: number column density (ncol) or COT (baer) 
.false.                 :save the layer AMFs                           
.false.                 :save the single and multiple scattering contributions 
 
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
AEROSOL PARAMETERS
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1                       :number of aerosol types (with index iaer)     
Mie_nrvar_ni0/S.sc.     :start name of file with aerosol single scattering expansion coefficients 
Mie_nrvar_ni0/S.lu.     :start name of file with LUT for aerosol single scattering matrix elements 
3601                    :number of scattering angles in the LUT between 0 and 180 degrees 
 
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
LAYER PARAMETERS (DEFINED AT LEVELS, NR OF LEVELS = nz+1)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1                       :number of absorbing gases                     
2                       :number of clouds (with index icloud)          
 
k_lev   alt (km)  pres (b)     temp (K)  O3 (ppm)  (ncol(icloud) or baer(icloud),iaer(icloud),ixmin(icloud),ixmax(icloud),iymin(icloud),iymax(icloud),icloud=1,nclouds)
